  "medSchoolCurriculum": {
    "medicalSchoolId": 27234,
    "dressCode": null,
    "tutoringPrograms": "Faculty maintain regular office hours and are also available to meet with students by appointments.",
    "globalExperience": 4,
    "patientInteraction": "Extensive patient interaction. Students participate in the 3-year Human Dimension course, partnering them with families in the community. Phase 1 also includes a Longitudinal Clinical Preceptorship.",
    "instructionStyle": "Our pre-clerkship curriculum is based on a blended model of active-learning with each week framed around a clinical case presentation that.  Pedagogies include TBL, PBL and laboratory sessions.",
    "clinicalRotations": null,
    "prematriculationProgram": "Please visit website",
    "rankStudents": "We do not currently conduct internal student rankings.",
    "lectureAttendance": "Lectures are mandatory. Students are expected to prepare prior to sessions and apply material in class.",
    "curricularHighlights": "The curriculum at the Hackensack Meridian School of Medicine is designed around our Vision: That each person in New Jersey, and in the US, regardless of race or socioeconomic status , will enjoy the highest levels of wellness in an economically and behaviorally sustainable fashion. The curriculum features a unique 3+1 design and an individualized 4th year.  Phase 1 is 16 months long and consists of fully integrated courses that weave together the biomedical, social, and health systems sciences.  Phase 2 is 20 months long and includes clerkships, followed by the Step 1 Exam, Advanced Clinical Rotations, and Step 2 Exams. During Phase 3, students select a personalized pathway possibly including a dual degree/certificate program, clinical immersion, research activities, community-based projects, or entry into residency. At the heart of the SOM curriculum is the Human Dimension course, which pairs students with families in the community over 3 years.",
    "primaryCarePrograms": "The Hackensack Meridian School of Medicine has a Mission that is focused on developing student-physicians who will deliver the highest quality care. While our Mission is not explicitly focused on developing primary care physicians, we have a strong commitment to primary care and anticipate that many of our graduates will pursue these fields. We expect our graduates will shape the healthcare system and workforce of the future to be one that:\n\u2022             Is not confined to the walls of hospitals or medical offices Seamlessly integrates with community-based activities and agencies\n\u2022             Utilizes advanced technologic and other systems to promote continuity, communication, and patient-centeredness\n\u2022             Has a physician workforce optimized to produce high quality, high value, equitable healthcare",
    "researchPrograms": "Our primary focus during the first five years of the School of Medicine will be to meet and exceed the expectations identified as necessary to achieve full Liaison Committee for Medical Education accreditation and more fundamentally, to create a school that in so doing will enable our graduates to truly realize the School of Medicine Vision.\n\nIn close collaboration with Hackensack Meridian Health, the School of Medicine will focus our primary research efforts as follows:\n\n1. Educational Research\n2.Behavioral Research\n3.Community-Based Research\n4. Health Services Research (\u201cbig data\u201d)\n",
